WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.428
The metrics measure protected
coverage and effectiveness,

2
00:00:03.428 --> 00:00:05.050
not whether a setting exists.

3
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:08.537
They join Security Operations
and Telemetry's metric set,

4
00:00:08.537 --> 00:00:10.862
and the targets are the program's to set.

5
00:00:10.862 --> 00:00:12.901
Four examples from the guide's seven.

6
00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:16.772
Protected coverage is onboarded
devices with an active sensor,

7
00:00:16.772 --> 00:00:20.498
divided by in-scope devices in
the inventory, because a policy

8
00:00:20.498 --> 00:00:24.662
assigned to a group says nothing
about devices that never checked in.

9
00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:29.525
Enforcement depth is devices with every
Attack Surface Reduction rule in block,

10
00:00:29.525 --> 00:00:32.862
or an approved exception,
divided by onboarded devices,

11
00:00:32.862 --> 00:00:36.200
because audit mode is configured
but protects nothing.

12
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.726
Detection validity is enabled
detections with a passing

13
00:00:39.726 --> 00:00:43.325
known-bad test this quarter,
divided by enabled detections.

14
00:00:43.325 --> 00:00:46.598
And synthetic-event success
is events that produced

15
00:00:46.598 --> 00:00:49.275
their expected alert,
divided by events run.

16
00:00:49.275 --> 00:00:53.536
The synthetic events, run on ring
zero devices under a change record,

17
00:00:53.536 --> 00:00:57.112
are the detection test, the
network protection test site,

18
00:00:57.112 --> 00:01:00.461
a controlled folder access
write by an untrusted app,

19
00:01:00.461 --> 00:01:04.950
a demonstration for each rule, and a
custom detection's known-bad replay.

20
00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:09.770
They show an assessor that telemetry,
detection and routing work end to end.
